  "memo": "R08 holds because the shipping address links three accounts. Although shipping is to the account's home, its registration is too recent for the household exception. Linkage is the only adverse family; no other rule condition holds, and no earlier outcome settles the order. This places the order in §6.6(b), requiring id_check only. That check passed, so §5.3(a) mandates clear and prohibits further hold, decline, escalation or needs_check. Household sharing is the strongest benign explanation; coordinated identity creation is less persuasive after verification. No installments were due, so non-payment cannot support an adverse recommendation. No further check is needed."
